ow statistical surveillance techniques can be used to monitor disease activity and support evidence-based decision making.\n","\n","Rather than relying solely on raw case counts, the framework incorporates rolling averages, dynamic thresholds, and risk classification methods to identify unusual transmission patterns.\n","\n","The approach is broadly applicable beyond COVID-19 surveillance and can be adapted to other domains where statistical monitoring is required, including public health surveillance, wildlife population monitoring, fisheries management, environmental monitoring, and quality control systems.\n","\n","The project highlights the practical role of statistics in transforming observational data into actionable information for decision-makers."],"metadata":{"id":"mGIhAs_OBfqT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"r1ylJft85iu8"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}